From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: katamaran <katamaran@localhost>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:04:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] tap: connect an in-process VM by function call

Built with -buildmode=c-shared, gvproxy can run inside the VMM process.
kat_gvproxy_start takes gvproxy's command line and the VMM's receive
function; kat_gvproxy_tx takes a frame from the guest. Frames then pass
by call both ways, without a socket or the thread hand-offs on each
side of it. Frames for the VM are written on the goroutine that made
them, as slices with a virtio-net header, and the link offloads TCP and
UDP checksums to the guest (NEEDS_CSUM with the pseudo-header sum).
